WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735
-You had your brother on stage,
which is great, and then,

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
of course, you also brought
Tommy on stage,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was one of the great
moments of the Globes.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.874 line:92%
He very clearly wanted to speak.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:08.608 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm surprised he didn't go
for the award.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- Yeah, I'm surprised.
Well, it's interesting.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.382 size:88% position:44%
This was -- You gave him
an interesting choice.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:18.251
If given a microphone or an
award, what would he go for,

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he went for the thing
that would amplify his voice.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Were you not the least

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
surprised that
he tried to speak?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.393 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-No, I'm not surprised.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, look, it's
a long time coming.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:33.400 size:84% position:42%
He kept saying to me --
'Cause like with Tommy,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.137
what he does, you know, if any
other person did what he does,

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would just end
in pure disaster.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:44.778
But he somehow always turns
disaster into something positive

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so here he is --
What I said,

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:52.719
there was, like, 19 years before
he had been, you know,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
stuck in limo traffic that
was going to the Globes

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was really upset
and it was one of the nights

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he actually turned
and was like, "You know what?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll show all them.
I'll make my own movie."

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.098
You know, and there he is,
19 years later on the stage.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really insane.
-And, he kept saying to me

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:11.204 size:78% position:39%
all night afterwards,
"It's destiny, James.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's destiny."

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really weird when things
go right for crazy people

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
because then --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.146
Then they think they're like --
-Believe me.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
Believe me.
Well, and that's one of

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.019
the magical things I loved about
this story is, it's an ironic

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:31.524
success slash tragedy where
his movie is still being watched

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
today 15 years later.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On the other hand,
as a creative person,

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
usually the way --
One of the ways you learn is,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
you try to do --
You're aiming for something,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.636
you make some mistakes, and you
realize, "Oh, I didn't go where

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to go, maybe
I should change some things."

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:47.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He did that.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:51.711
He's trying to make a drama on
the level of Tennessee Williams,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he made a comedy, so that
became a success

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.618
and then he flipped the switch
and said I intend to do comedy,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:02.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he'll never learn
from the mistakes he made.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
And I think it's probably not

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
a great sign that he hasn't --
Has he made a second film?

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, if you go
the screening.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
He made this show
called "Neighbors,"

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.337 line:92%
and he's trying to be funny.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.507
We went and did a special
screening of "The Room"

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:24.477 size:75% position:38%
for our film to play
during the credit.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's supposed to start
at midnight.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:31.284
It started at 2:30 A.M. because
he hocks his underwear,

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:35.088
it says Tommy Wiseau underwear,
his T.W., as he call them.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Right, he puts them on

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
people in the lobby and
they come model them on stage.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:45.431
And then he shows, not one, but
every episode of "Neighbors."

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, boy.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:49.202 size:88% position:44%
So I fell asleep in that
screening of "The Room."

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You nailed "The Voice,"
and we were saying

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we were talking
about the film earlier --

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
People, when you first --
If you haven't seen "The Room"

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.481
when you see this character,
it's a very big swing from you,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it is actually
incredibly accurate.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.384 size:84% position:42%
And you tried very hard
to get the voice right.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You had recordings of him?

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
So, like I said, Tommy --

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have the recordings
right here.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:15.862
Okay, Tommy flipped the switch
after he realized that people

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
were laughing at it and said,
I intended to be comedy.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I couldn't really --
So he had rewritten history,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.603 size:88% position:44%
so I couldn't really go
to him and ask him about

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
what he was like during
"The Room" because he'd just

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
give me, "Oh, well, I intended
this to be funny."

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:33.079 size:78% position:39%
But he used to record
himself all the time.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.382
He would drive around in his car
and talk to himself on

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
a mini tape recorder.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:41.387
This is, like, five years before
"The Room," 20 years ago.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:44.090 size:78% position:39%
His good friend Greg,
as good friends do,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
stole some of these tapes
way back when.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, when I was going
to get ready for it,

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.864 size:81% position:41%
he had digitized them
and he sent them to me

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:55.301 size:84% position:42%
and they're incredible.
It's Tommy, you know,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
complaining about
acting teachers

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:02.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can see --
It was like I got his journal

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:06.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the audio book version and
so here's a little thing.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-This is him talking about

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
an acting teacher.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Inaudible ]

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.794
That was okay, but again, I had
an argument with him as usual.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Again, as usual.
As usual.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:27.467
-This time was, he said,
"Why don't you do the same thing

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
in French."
It's so stupid.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what
his problem is.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.341 line:92%
I know what his problem is.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he knows
I'm very powerful.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
He can feel it.
This power.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You see that?

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's been Tommy Wiseau
the whole time.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-He's been him the whole time.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, congratulations
on the film.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:55.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for talking with me
about everything today

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I hope to see you soon.
All right.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.032 size:88% position:44% line:92%
James Franco, everybody.

